Subject: Cantor SJS Compiled Lookahead Repository Stitch Projection P0 Requirements Analysis

@ [requirements_analysis_uuid] fd96e610-6152-417e-ade5-064f645cb2b0
@ [canonical_uuid] fc3a2e9e-1fc5-4b04-a867-431c2ab0584f

& [Necessary]
  + RSO ends with a verified candidate-selection envelope while the stitch compiler begins with a separately supplied declaration request
  + an exact typed adapter is necessary before repository-derived selections can become the scope-persistent stitch packet intended for inference-host consumption
  + upstream verification must precede projection or unverified repository claims could be laundered into stitch declarations
  + field-for-field mapping and deterministic identity derivation are necessary to prevent new semantic generation inside the adapter

& [SufficientForP0]
  + exact upstream triplet replay selected-only mapping one-hint declarations one activation each one initial projection and downstream verifier replay support a provider-free projection receipt
  + separate historical physical-contact and current zero-effect accounts preserve honest composition

& [NotSufficient]
  + a compiled stitch packet does not authorize prompt insertion provider invocation model inference quality claims autonomous continuation or workspace effects
